    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93895" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σηστός</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σήθω</span>) nickname of the courtesan Phryne, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the sifter</i>, because she
			drained her lovers of money, Herodic. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				13.591c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σηστὸν καρύων Ποντικῶν</span>, perh.
			name of a measure, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				13.22
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				12.9
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>.</div>
